<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cilmeri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cilmery</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cilmeri is a village near Builth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">Wells</a> in Powys, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. On 11 December 1282 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a>, the last native <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, was killed nearby in a clash with English forces, and his death led to Edward I's conquest of Wales. A granite memorial stone raised on the site in 1956 has become a place of remembrance for Welsh nationalists.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cilmeri.jpg" alt="Cilmeri" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philip Halling · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monument_to_Prince_Llywelyn_-_geograph.org.uk_-_250372.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
